 EMPIRE CODE PARAMETRIZATION                                      2634 1451
 ---------------------------                                      2634 1451
                                                                  2634 1451
 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   2634 1451
 (SVN rev.  4977; source rev.  4977)                              2634 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [8,9].                                       2634 1451
                                                                  2634 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 2634 1451
  NDNUC= 160  NDEXCLUS= 50  NDEX= 241  NDLW= 100                  2634 1451
  LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        2634 1451
                                                                  2634 1451
 The following EMPIRE-code modules and features were used in      2634 1451
 the current evaluation:                                          2634 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2634 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      2634 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  2634 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                2634 1451
   and coworkers                                                  2634 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2634 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          2634 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 2634 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2634 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2634 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2634 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2634 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2634 1451
   discrete transitions                                           2634 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [10]                  2634 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2634 1451
   level density, discrete levels,                                2634 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2634 1451
   library [13]                                                   2634 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2634 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  2634 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     2634 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2634 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2634 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      2634 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   2634 1451
                                                                  2634 1451
                      EMPIRE options                              2634 1451
                      --------------                              2634 1451
 Following options and deviations from the default values of      2634 1451
 the parameters were employed in the EMPIRE calculations:         2634 1451
                                                                  2634 1451
 - CC calculations using soft-rotor omp for the incident channel. 2634 1451
 - CN decay and Direct cross sections added incoherently.         2634 1451
 - Traditional Hauser-Feschbach Tlj_{CC}(E)=Tlj_{GS}(E-Egs).      2634 1451
 - HRTW width fluctuation correction calculated  up to 9.90 MeV.  2634 1451
 - Tlj coupling for the top CN bin  up to incident  9.90 MeV.     2634 1451
 - CN anisotropy calculated using Blatt-Biedenharn coefficients.  2634 1451
 - Coupled Channels Method used for Tl calcul. in outgoing ch.    2634 1451
 - Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3+                    2634 1451
    library based on the 2015 version of ENSDF.                   2634 1451
 - Gamma-transition multipolarity set to 2.                       2634 1451
 - GDR parameters taken from RIPL/Exp.data+Plujko systematics.    2634 1451
 - E1 strength function set to RIPL MLO1                          2634 1451
 - Gilbert-Cameron (EMPIRE 2.18) level densities.                 2634 1451
 - Preequilibrium mechanism treated in terms of the exciton model 2634 1451
    with the Iwamoto-Harada model for emission of clusters, and   2634 1451
    Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)        2634 1451
